Task: Implement TypeScript wrappers for stable kernel operations

Summary:
- Added the TypeScript bridge layer for stable kernel operations: discovery, fit, predict, simulate, summarize, and diagnose.
- Normalized kernel bridge responses into idiomatic TypeScript objects and mapped bridge failures to a typed KernelBridgeError.
- Exported the wrapper surface and helper types from the package entrypoint.
- Added coverage for the wrapper flow and bridge error normalization.

Files:
- bindings/typescript/src/kernel.ts
- bindings/typescript/src/index.ts
- bindings/typescript/src/bridge.ts
- bindings/typescript/test/kernel-wrappers.test.ts
- bindings/typescript/test/kernel-bridge.test.ts

Validation:
- npm run typecheck
- npx vitest run --no-cache --coverage

Why:
- This creates the stable TypeScript surface on top of the existing Python kernel bridge so consumers can use the kernel without dealing with the lower-level request/response protocol directly.
